---
title: "G8 Verify, data and diagnostics: where each testbench fake enters the real pipeline, the verify run's lease, the recorders and their upload, report.sh, doctor.sh, the logs, the tour (78e93b1, G8Verify.tla, FakeWornGuard.tla copy)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    direction LR
    lg0: Off, not running, or the real input with nothing faked
    lg1: The real pipeline or a tool running as it should
    lg2: Between: a lease running out, a stand-in going stale, a gate checking
    lg3: A fake in place: an override, a stand-in file, a parked tracker, a held lock
    lg4: Suspected open bug: the state that breaks the rule
    lg5: V1 open, OverridesEnd and WearerGetsReal: the input proxy's overrides (worn on or off, head pose, HMD buttons, synthetic controllers) have no time limit, and a real wearer doesn't end them (input_state.cpp 112-116). Only T release, V cleanup or a SteamVR restart do (cli.py 351-363). A run whose agent dies keeps them, and its guard keeps every input host's lock. The lease only marks the run stale (verify-frametop 91, 169). Someone who puts the headset on later gets a frozen head pose, or standby under worn off (red V1.1-5, TLC Overrides, 5 steps then a loop, OverridesFix holds)
    lg6: V2 open, FakesEnd: the fake trackers end after an hour with no command (fakes.py 47, 815), but any command restarts the hour, status too (836-837). T status sends one, so every V doctor, V guard and MCP status does. A later agent's doctor checks keep a dead run's fake eyes and parked hands alive, and without them they still last up to an hour (red V2.1-2, TLC Code and Polls, 7 to 9 steps then a loop, Fixed holds)
    lg7: V3 open, minor, GuardRestoresReal on the FakeWornGuard copy with fairness: a guard that dies while the input proxy stalls. after_guard tries the release 3 times 0.2 s apart, then gives up (hostinput.py 209-217, 230-237). The faked wearer stays until the next T command. NoHostTakeover still holds: the flag stops ft-stream (red V3.1-2, TLC LiveNoF and LiveAll break, LiveKills and LiveHangs hold)
    lg8: V4 open, minor, G3 side: in pointer mode the relay's drop of the testbench mouse lets go of its buttons only on the virtual mouse (release_held, input-relay.py 1654-1659). A testbench killed mid-drag, or a release read after hostbye, leaves the 3D mouse's button down until the next click. Written up in testbench/docs/desktop.md Limits. Same class as G3 K7 (red V4.1-2, not modelled)
    lg9: V5 open, minor, moot at 78e93b1: the hand upload's draft gate opens on FT_HANDREC_ALLOW_UPLOAD=1 alone (hands/rec/hub.py 91-94), the eye one only for another dataset (gaze/rec/hub.py 60-62). is_draft counts a missing text as final (recorder/hub.py 47-52). All five texts are final now (red V5.1-2, not modelled)
    lg10: Holds at 78e93b1: TypeOK, LaunchClean and NoDriveOnWearer in all 6 G8Verify configs (26 to 98 states), every rule in NoDeath (a live agent always cleans up) and Fixed. FakeWornGuard copy: NoHostTakeover and FakeIsNoticed in Clean 88, Hangs 188, Kills 264, NoF 480 and All 632 states, the skill's baseline. GuardRestoresReal in LiveClean, LiveHangs and LiveKills
    lg11: Fixed before 78e93b1, green arrows: A 37d0fbf, worn on dropped the flag after a reply timeout. B ft-stream bd606ce (merge 81a5c82), a SIGKILLed guard freed the lock before the wearer went. C 37d0fbf, drop_unsafe_worn took a timeout for no proxy. D 0c7eb9e, start_guard cleared an unconfirmed-release flag. E 38d6257, a stale worn answer. F 1f485fe, the guard stopped between start_guard and the post-check
    lg12: Escape hatches: V1, T release, V cleanup --force, or a SteamVR restart (only through testbench/install.sh). V2, T release or stopping frame-testbench-fakes. V3, any T command. V4, one click. V5, leave the variable unset
    lg13: Another group: arrows into it are where a fake or a tool enters it, drawn there, not here
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 yellow
